From 44cb45dd0a7d8892bcb29b28a5478876ecdafeaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kgursu <kgursu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:08:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] FsCrypt: skip restorecon of CE paths in recovery

fscrypt_prepare_user_storage() ran RestoreconRecursive() over
/data/system_ce/<user>, /data/vendor_ce/<user> and /data/misc_ce/<user>
after the CE key was installed. The recovery's Android 12 libselinux
does not apply the per-user MLS level (s0:c512,c768 for user 0) that
Android 14+ uses for misc_ce/<user>/checkin and sdksandbox, so every
recovery session that decrypted CE storage relabelled them to s0.

On the next unlock vold_prepare_subdirs cannot relabel checkin from s0
(policy allows relabelto, not relabelfrom). LineageOS 23.2 then leaves
sys.user.0.ce_available unset and apps cannot create their Android/data
directories; LineageOS 24 deletes and recreates the directory.

Recovery has no need to relabel these paths; Android does it at unlock.
Tested on SM-T970 (LineageOS 24): after a CE-decrypting session the
checkin label and inode stay unchanged and no Relabelling lines appear.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LV7KkPo6rUamzmMaty3K2W
---
 FsCrypt.cpp | 13 +++++--------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FsCrypt.cpp b/FsCrypt.cpp
index 7505e56..9373ec1 100644
--- a/FsCrypt.cpp
+++ b/FsCrypt.cpp
@@ -913,14 +913,11 @@ bool fscrypt_prepare_user_storage(const std::string& volume_uuid, userid_t user_
             if (!EnsurePolicy(ce_policy, user_ce_path)) return false;
         }
 
-        if (volume_uuid.empty()) {
-            // Now that credentials have been installed, we can run restorecon
-            // over these paths
-            // NOTE: these paths need to be kept in sync with libselinux
-            android::vold::RestoreconRecursive(system_ce_path);
-            android::vold::RestoreconRecursive(vendor_ce_path);
-            android::vold::RestoreconRecursive(misc_ce_path);
-        }
+        // Recovery: no restorecon over system_ce, vendor_ce and misc_ce here.
+        // The recovery libselinux does not know the per-user MLS level that
+        // newer Android versions give to directories such as
+        // misc_ce/<user>/checkin and sdksandbox, and would relabel them to s0.
+        // Android relabels these paths itself when the user is unlocked.
     }
     if (!prepare_subdirs("prepare", volume_uuid, user_id, flags)) return false;
 
